  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Area Approximations: trapezoidal rule for a curve</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.2 (b) / Essential 2.1 (b): Find the strip width and the ordinates of a quadratic curve and estimate the area under it with the trapezoidal rule and 4 strips.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Exercise C, Question 4 in Chapter 9 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: completing a table of ordinates, then the rule; new polynomial curves and intervals.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
